{"step_index":838,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T04:39:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-10T12:39:09+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-10T12:39:14+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-10T12:39:09+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-10T12:39:14+08:00\nThe search for \"window.crypto.subtle file:// protocol origin null secure context chrome firefox safari\" returned the following summary:\nWhen you open an HTML file directly from your local file system using the **`file://` protocol** (e.g., double-clicking an `.html` file or typing `file:///path/to/file.html` into your browser address bar), browsers treat the origin as **`null`**[1]. \n\nBecause `file://` / `null` origin is **not** considered a secure context, **`window.crypto.subtle` will be `undefined`** (or throw errors when used) across modern browsers like Chrome, Firefox, and Safari[2][3].\n\n---\n\n### Why does this happen?\nThe Web Crypto API (`window.crypto.subtle`) provides powerful low-level cryptographic functions[4]. Per the W3C Web Cryptography specification and browser security policies, these features are restricted to **Secure Contexts** to prevent malicious scripts from arbitrarily handling sensitive cryptographic keys or data[2][5]. \n* **Secure contexts** are defined as pages delivered via **HTTPS**, or locally via **`localhost` / `127.0.0.1`**[2][3].\n* The **`file://` protocol** lacks a secure origin concept (mapping to an opaque origin of `null`), meaning browsers disable `crypto.subtle` entirely[3][1].\n\n---\n\n### Browser Behavior Matrix (`file://` protocol)\n\n| Browser | Behavior with `file://` (`crypto.subtle`) | Console Error / Symptom |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Google Chrome / Edge** | `window.crypto.subtle` is **`undefined`**[5][3] | `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'digest' / 'encrypt' / etc.)`[3] |\n| **Mozilla Firefox** | `window.crypto.subtle` is **`undefined`**[3] | `TypeError: window.crypto.subtle is undefined`[3] |\n| **Apple Safari** | `window.crypto.subtle` may be undefined or throw security/secure-context exceptions depending on the OS/Safari version. | Restricted due to lack of secure context. |\n\n---\n\n### How \n<truncated 1388 bytes>\nGkHpDLtEQdIlXLLptLzA9a52E21-rACYplLsdoQHITfgCrn_ecytxHgx1OP764dziOH7b6ihwBMbU6-aW5gcy9PWobHGwYyi7SoNKGJxPj_c7tYdy-JCv0XodBUoKPE1aXCRmAfLPURA_8lereEYF6dg==)\n[3] [authgear.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_jUMFZRX0m39qIx_2WKPwgdZCPPKJc2W81gCIc05Mrlwy4Mk9OCqErZgiQqA6PZshmqZOCgU-Lg-NncaW_PhZV9fI9u9r3GASrriE8YjNSjtL-zkMCg7pURDxnpGA7p20vSSd0JaarDVRajoXz8y5j6hptcnGdRZDCxFR9xkyzqtSLr7VDOjk2kccbCrEAQjApi1_by2gIWu-wBftrg==)\n[4] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjGHrYSobaTc77cEqOHGYtCwSVpIQ_MxelnSref1hv8ldR84WLm4lB5XdKZLvaQ-6HNsZTzxZz6FpjqkNOUUtXEPWbuVnjGT02g40uk4LdpqY9OX2BFTzUT-5NUiEtn4BjWEeJZTGINn5Eflae5Io1EbQZ)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHrZ5q8_q7ODAfhrSifhYctNjsthTfM5GLpjYSgol66fDyyz3bTgrv2IxqotSjpZNpTZRer9VFF-jYOnghizMT8h1F6aF4k9F9UOuAkQJEgCkp6h7Zt2zNyITCNitDPKR8NBcw_KvihNkpX-XQstEwtb4mm1fRI-Qz8K1SYZTkoR2FFWsXwGI45KTUP9jOFo3ERmWLXVUEUr5snYmpmdJeI1w9Dd13)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrK0MU32IiXgqKaItVmjq38yihJi_S2fCFebMOzI-U7w2Ko2M74vQbGV2AKKNdM5fDv3G5aRNsxOaiefhdcbKvTxJcNhD-bbuiGELzDFTzJ9A3mV-JQeOEqpEz8BMEM-wb-uB3VHASp81hsMmO-cjl6xFLxGxoKtODZTnVxL9fkO9p9FoJiDfHXU7yqchAsuCbVuZ-3uYuPSZxf0MT0QQwr3iMNg4mUA==)\n[7] [freecodecamp.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCP6Or9WU232Pby8lZmGIR4BTGq5TbFr_cD1TYp0_Hc49UNnYhA3sxYbUPHLzGdkvu8txjWtGopgPZtlxo4BBe4YL-IAiQfPzw-otjoYb0RE1MjL1Skd5k5zorCmh8tmxiytrJW-p4SMXrVf0txKgdvBTWOjutrKPZB6YDsnUQ235C9-y7Sa39nxlV1zQeveNFSuhIdsXwHoacVazJ6z8fq79VvE83lJl3KtDgLUL5fBo=)\n[8] [webnots.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQExXX4OL-cQKsz2-